Subject: ksmserver -- launch the desktop directly (twin/kicker/kdesktop)

ksmserver normally launches session apps (window manager, panel, desktop) by an
async DCOP exec_blind() to tdelauncher and sequences kdesktop/kicker through the
DCOP-coordinated autostart phases.  On substrate the autostart-phase handshake
(tdelauncher's autoStartNDone() signals back to ksmserver) does not reliably
complete, so the session can stall before the panel/desktop come up.

Launch the core desktop directly instead: startApplication() fork()+execvp()s the
command (binaries are on $PATH under /opt/trinity/bin), and restoreSession()/
startDefaultSession() also start kdesktop and kicker directly.  Inter-app DCOP
itself works (the af_unix SO_PEERCRED fix) so exec_blind would also launch the
app -- but doing both races two copies of the same unique app past each other, so
this uses fork()+execvp() as the single launch path; the autostart's later
duplicate is dropped by TDEUniqueApplication's defer-to-running check (tdelibs
patch 0009).

--- a/ksmserver/server.cpp
+++ b/ksmserver/server.cpp
@@ -118,10 +118,26 @@
     }
     int n = command.count();
     TQCString app = command[0].latin1();
-    TQValueList<TQCString> argList;
-    for ( int i=1; i < n; i++)
-       argList.append( TQCString(command[i].latin1()));
-    DCOPRef( launcher ).send( "exec_blind", app, DCOPArg( argList, "TQValueList<TQCString>" ) );
+
+    /* substrate: launch session apps (the window manager, panel, desktop, ...)
+     * directly with fork()+execvp() rather than the async DCOP exec_blind() to
+     * tdelauncher.  Inter-app DCOP now works (the af_unix SO_PEERCRED fix), so
+     * exec_blind would also launch the app — but doing BOTH races two copies of
+     * the same unique app past each other (each registers before it sees the
+     * other), and the tdelauncher/autostart start_service path does not reliably
+     * bring up kdesktop here.  fork()+execvp() is the single reliable path; the
+     * autostart's later duplicate is dropped by TDEUniqueApplication's
+     * defer-to-running check.  Binaries are on $PATH (/opt/trinity/bin). */
+    if ( fork() == 0 ) {
+        setsid();
+        char **argv = (char **) malloc( ( n + 1 ) * sizeof( char * ) );
+        argv[0] = strdup( app.data() );
+        for ( int i = 1; i < n; i++ )
+            argv[i] = strdup( command[i].latin1() );
+        argv[n] = 0;
+        execvp( argv[0], argv );
+        _exit( 127 );
+    }
 }
 
